Our fix for the endless loop in lib/xarray.c xa_store_range() when
last == ULONG_MAX, against v7.1 (unchanged in v7.3 and linux-next as of
2026-10-22).  The tiling loop adds each stored chunk's size to `first`
while first <= last; the chunk that ends at ULONG_MAX wraps `first` to 0,
and 0 <= ULONG_MAX holds, so the loop never ends.  Stop when `first`
wraps: a range that does not end at ULONG_MAX leaves first = last + 1,
non-zero, so nothing else changes.  INCOMPLETE (2026-11-07, see README):
[0, ULONG_MAX] then returns with ULONG_MAX unstored.  Apply with
`git -C <tree> apply` and rebuild the harness to see it.

--- a/lib/xarray.c
+++ b/lib/xarray.c
@@ -1896,7 +1896,7 @@
 			if (xas_error(&xas))
 				goto unlock;
 			first += xas_size(&xas);
-		} while (first <= last);
+		} while (first && first <= last);
 unlock:
 		xas_unlock(&xas);
 	} while (xas_nomem(&xas, gfp));
